WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.830
<i>A feeling she had wanted to convey for so long, and was finally able to. {## implied second 'convey', and it's the same verb anyway}</i>

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:16.240
<i>A feeling that pierced this world, slowly being drowned and sealed off in a sea of sorrow, like a ray of light.</i>

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:22.770
But even if that happens, I alone will stay by your side. {## i'm just gonna trust that you checked these}

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:30.000
From now on, you and I will be together forever and ever.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.070
<i>A strong feeling.</i>

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.310
Mato-chan.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.890
Thank you.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:42.860
Farewell.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.060
<i>Her feelings reached him,</i>

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.570
<i>so why does he choose to remain alone?</i>

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:53.180
<i>Is he fine not meeting her again? 
Are </i>you<i> fine with that, Mato-chan?</i>

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.710
<i>Or is it that you've already forgotten it all?</i>

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.570
<i>My feelings...</i>

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.300
Continuing a dream?

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.880
Is it dangerous? {## why would it be dangerous my dude}

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.590
I don't know. I don't know, but...

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.390
Ane-chan-senpai, we'll fully support you on all fronts.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:20.880
You can count on us! {## for the single isolated incident what this is}

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:25.860
Thanks.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:33.240
There's so much I wanted to talk to you about

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:33.240
hanashitakatta koto takusan atta no ni

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:38.580
But my mind went blank when I saw your face

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:38.580
kao miru to wasurechau

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:47.190
Every time you peek in to pick me up after school my heart lights up

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:47.190
houkago mukae ni kitekureru no ga ureshikute

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:54.440
I wonder why I so hopelessly feel this way about you

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:54.440
doushite kimi ja nakucha dame na no kana

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:08.190
Maybe it's like how we can't live without the sun or sea

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:08.190
taiyou ya mizu ga hitsuyou na no to niteru ki ga suru

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:15.580
The days have begun to get shorter now

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:15.580
hi ga mijikaku nattekita ne

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:23.710
Why must they cut off my time with you?

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:23.710
mou chotto issho ni itai no ni

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:29.320
Tomorrow and the day after, and every day forevermore

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:29.320
ashita mo asatte mo sono saki mo zutto

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:34.470
I want to keep walking home together like this

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:34.470
kouyatte kimi to kaeritai

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:39.920
No matter what the weather was, no matter how my day went

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:39.920
donna tenki demo donna kibun demo

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:47.690
The moment you raise your hand to wave goodbye

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:47.690
mata ne to kimi ga te wo furu toki

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:55.670
I feel like it has been a wonderful day

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:55.670
ii hi datta to omoeru kara

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:03.870
Right, think back and slowly remember each part of the dream you had.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:09.830
Imagine yourself in the dream again, with each detail becoming clearer.

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:14.300
Paint a picture of the moment when the dream was cut off. {## supports a pause before 'when'}

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.810
Heck yeah! {## heck is not a joke word / ugh, whatever}

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.240
I made it back!

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:36.520
Yay!

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:37.930
What?!

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:39.730
So, what should we do next?

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:42.930
Wait, wait, wait, wait! What are you two doing here?

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.200
Um, we were wondering about that Peter person... {## or quotes around Peter but I feel like you'd kill it / anyway otherwise it sounds like they know him}

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:48.610
Peter!

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:56.740
Is he perhaps someone you can only meet inside a dream?

00:03:56.740 --> 00:04:02.540
And once we got to thinking, we figured there might be something we could do to help you out in here! {## orig. reads as 'help you (out here)', but a dream would be 'in here'}

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:06.220
So that's why you followed me into my dream?

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.180
I'm not sure we'll be much help...{## apart from obvious cool literal arguments, saying 'we can't help' means Teko's already convinced of that (and it happens to be untrue)}

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:14.810
But we want to follow through on fully supporting you on all fronts!

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:18.020
That's great and all, but what about back in reality?

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:22.350
What would people think of three high school girls fast asleep on a stairway? {## isn't this actually fine though, given the circumstances}

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:23.740
We've got that covered!

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:27.150
Otouto-kun-senpai is on guard duty for us.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:34.330
I guess I can accept that. And since you're here, let's go all out and— {## when adverbial like this, no hyphen / I CHECKED}

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.080
Advisor Cha and Ohime! {## why does he flip twice without any sort of scene marker, it's so weird, i thought I was losing my mind}

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:50.590
They're here too!

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:53.130
Can't do much if they're already here. {## 'no helping it if' / oh, avoiding double help i see}

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:55.890
I'm gonna have every single one of you help me out!

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.880
Our objective is the sailing ship in the air! {## that's definitely not a boat, aka / just 'flying ship'}

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.400
All right, let's fly!

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.420
Okay!

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.700
A net?!

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:12.160
Don't worry. Brooms aren't for flying, they're just for steering, right? {## this wasn't a quote, was it?}

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.230
A net is just as good.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:20.640
All right!

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:23.170
Go!

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:29.760
Ane-chan-senpai, you're very skilled.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:32.030
I learned it from you.

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:33.770
Plus, this is my second time.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:40.900
It's huge!

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:48.450
Ane-chan-senpai!

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:52.790
Thanks, Tekochin. {## I think this could arguably be Th-Th, but whatever}

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:02.250
Ane-chan-senpai, look out!

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:07.840
Are you okay, Ane-chan-senpai?

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.220
Yeah!

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:20.150
Advisor Cha! Ohime!

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:25.400
Thank goodness.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:30.740
Over there! Peter should be inside.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:35.240
It's closing!

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:44.450
Nice, Advisor Cha!

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:46.130
Ane-chan-senpai, hurry!

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:53.050
Pikari! Tekochin!

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.760
Made it!

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.300
Good luck!

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:00.370
Thank you.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:24.540
I'm back, Peter!

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:26.930
Ai?!

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.520
But how... {## I read this as more of another 'why' but it's not like it matters}

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:31.680
Why are you here?

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:33.480
I thought I told you.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:36.950
This world will soon be completely sealed off.

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:38.140
This kind of world...

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:41.100
This kind of world isn't worth hurting Mato-chan over. {makikomu is a more general word}

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:47.570
That's why you bid farewell to her, even after she said she'd stay with you forever.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:51.690
You asked me why I came back, right?

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:53.530
You don't know?

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:58.070
It's the same reason Mato-chan came here again and again.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:01.770
The same feeling she had when she said she'll stay with you forever.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.670
The feeling of love.

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:09.380
The feeling of love?

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:11.010
That's right!

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:13.010
Who feels it for who? {no need for whom here}{## oh dear, you read me like a book. it really should be 'whom', though}

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.930
Me! And I'm saying I love <i>you</i>! {## after like all of ten minutes with this dude? come on, Ane}{it was actually months}

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:28.230
Uh, what was I saying...

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:29.360
Oh, right.

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:33.290
You should understand that feeling too, Peter.

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:37.330
After all, the reason you said goodbye to Mato-chan...

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:39.900
was because of it too.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:43.120
Love?

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:47.040
Is that what I feel?

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:56.010
Yes. That's right. {## this was goofy shit}

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:04.850
Hey. {## not this though, this was great}

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:09.320
Peter, what would happen to you if you woke up? {## will when wake, would if woke}

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.430
I'd return to being a baby.

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:16.280
In the real world, I'm but a powerless baby.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:25.740
Neverland is a bubble-like dream shown by a mysterious black cat sleeping snuggled up next to that baby.

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:32.080
That's why I can't stay with either of you.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:37.520
I won't say I'll do something like stay with you.

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:42.430
I'm different from Mato-chan! {## for the nth time}

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.640
Come on and open your eyes, Peter!

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:49.360
Open your eyes and scream and cry!

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:52.860
That way, someone might come and find you.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:56.820
Your mother might even come back for you!

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:01.770
I believe it was snowing.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:08.900
A baby abandoned at a shrine would just freeze to death like that.

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:12.420
Don't worry.

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:16.880
From the very start, I was alone in this world. {it's like this for sure}

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:23.500
But thanks to all of the people who visited me, 
I was able to make more than enough memories.

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:32.280
So even if this place is completely closed off, I'll just be returning to how I used to live.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:36.470
Ai, believe me. {## EYES ARE TOO BIG}

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:38.760
I'll be fine.

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:46.910
Peter, you liar.

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:51.430
As if you'll be fine. {## 'Saying you'll be fine.', literally anything else}

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:52.810
Look closely.

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:57.920
The water is coming out from this stone baby.

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:01.930
It's crying, "I'm lonely, I'm lonely." {## I forgot what Fowler had to say about this, but seems fine}

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:05.140
This isn't ordinary water. {## 'isn't just' means 'is, but is also ...', but this isn't ordinary water at all}

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:10.080
It's the tears that have been pouring from your heart since you gained consciousness.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:19.070
Tell me, this is where Neverland all started, isn't it? {## 'origin of where you created' is just messed up / who cares about 'anata ga umidashita', not meee}

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:20.530
Yeah.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:24.990
If you were able to start it, 
doesn't that mean you can end it too? {## don't like 'create ... end', should be 'create ... destroy'. double start pref, and it's not like they're diff. Japanese}

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:26.910
Then let's do it!

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:34.680
Ai?

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.460
Ai...

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:42.990
The place it all started was our town, just a little bit in the past.

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:48.370
I'm not sure exactly how many years ago 
that was, but we're still in the same town.

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:51.330
That's why...

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:54.200
I'm sure we'll meet again.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:58.620
That's why... we have to do this. {## euh, but if we have it here we don't need it in the next, at least}

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:04.760
Your suffering and sadness in solitude... has to end. {## the ellipsis placement was way too weird}

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:08.830
Please wake up!

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:14.210
Do you really think... we'll meet again? {## I know it's eru, but no one would say this}

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:22.260
Huh? Um, are you talking about Mato-chan?

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:25.140
Oh, or maybe you mean your mom.

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:30.100
Either way, once you wake up, start crying hysterically.

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:34.560
Don't worry. You'll meet again.

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:39.070
Dreams fade from memory with time.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:46.240
Ai, I'm sure that everything you saw here, everything you said,

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:50.600
and even my existence will be forgotten too.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:55.370
I won't forget.

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:00.550
I'll never forget!

00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:02.820
Ai?

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:13.930
Got it.

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:17.150
That's enough, Cait Sith. {## really Cat Sith or Cat Sidhe or Cat Si, but whatever, I played Final Fantasy}

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:18.800
Thanks for everything.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:26.850
All right, guess it's time to wake up!

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:44.340
Peter, it's a promise!

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:47.090
We have to meet again!

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:51.650
Even if you forget, I'll come and find you!

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:55.670
Even if it takes until I turn old and gray, 
I'll find you no matter what!

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:00.890
Okay, Ai.

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:02.450
I promise!

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:04.280
Yeah.

00:14:05.100 --> 00:14:06.260
It's a promise.

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:13.820
Thank you, Ai.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:29.760
Huh?

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.370
Are you awake? {## this is such a stupid question when I think about it but I would say it too}

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:37.410
Teko-chan and Pikari-chan went back to their classroom.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:47.950
I feel like I had a really strange dream.

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:53.620
A strange, kind of sad, and kind of happy dream.

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:55.970
I see. {## what's Otouto supposed to say here? poor guy}

00:14:57.650 --> 00:15:01.010
I have to go finish preparing for the festival.

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:06.590
<i>What is this?</i>

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:10.930
<i>It feels like I'm forgetting something important... {## water step is 10/10}</i>

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:25.400
Mato-cha—

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:51.090
<i>Didn't I tell you? I'll never forget!</i>

00:15:59.490 --> 00:16:01.230
Mato-chan-sensei.

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:03.380
Ane-chan.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:06.690
Peter won't be appearing around here anymore.

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:10.800
He made me a promise.

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.610
He's going to wake up.

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:20.550
From that bubble-like dream world of a powerless baby, Neverland. {## i don't think 'bubble' is really necessary here, though}

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:24.790
Neverland...

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:30.810
After you had to part ways with him, I was able to go one more time.

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:34.550
And I made him promise me that.

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:45.620
I see.

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:50.650
My memories grew vague with the passage of time...

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:55.950
At some point I became convinced that it was all made up. {## despite the fact that you're on patrol every year because this dude kidnaps your students? hello?}

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.400
I see.

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:02.580
He finally managed to open his eyes.

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:04.240
I'm glad.

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:11.760
That black cat...

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:14.860
Isn't that the one who was always with him?

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:16.840
Huh? Is it?

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:24.240
Doesn't it look like he wants us to follow him? {## I understand that it's the same sasou, but this is dumb}

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:26.940
Huh?!

00:17:27.590 --> 00:17:28.900
Finished!

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:30.560
Only two left!

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:32.150
Final spurt!

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:35.320
Let's-a go! {## IT'S-A ME}

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:48.130
This shrine...

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:52.310
Yeah, it's where Neverland started.

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:09.020
Towano...sensei? {## HOLY FUCKING SHIT so THIS is why he didn't have eyes}

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:10.760
What a letdown.

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:11.600
I was sure—

00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:15.240
Do you want to know what happened to Peter?

00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:17.340
How?

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:18.450
After that,

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:30.380
his mother came back for him right away.

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:36.840
It seems that he was only abandoned for a very short moment. {## nice going, stretching that into a literal dream eternity}

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:41.600
After that, he lived a normal life and grew into an adult.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:47.060
By the time he started to work, he was convinced that Neverland was just a dream.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:53.520
But after meeting Katori-sensei, fragments of memories started returning bit by bit.

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:57.240
And then suddenly, I saw something unforgettable.

00:18:57.890 --> 00:18:59.140
Ninomiya Ai.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:03.160
It was your vibrant blue stripes. {what, no comment?}

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:07.790
The blue stripes Peter saw during the school festival.

00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:12.630
The blue stripes Towano Mamoru accidentally got a peek of.

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:19.380
When I saw those exact same blue stripes a second time, 
I realized that my time in Neverland was real.

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:23.050
I no longer have any doubt. {## first this was inappropriate because this JK was in love with a literal baby, and now it's inappropriate because she's in love with her homeroom teacher?}

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:26.440
Stop saying "blue stripes, blue stripes" over and over again!

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:29.100
Stupid Homeroom! Stupid Peter!

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:29.850
Like you said...

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:33.270
we met again. {## one sent}

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:37.170
Yeah.

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:45.080
Mato-chan-sensei!

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:49.800
Come on, you're stiff as a board!

00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:51.900
Go, go, go, go!

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:55.460
Take as much time as you need.

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:57.660
See you!

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:07.870
Are you really...

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:12.640
The real... Peter?

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:16.770
If you can accept my being an old man now. {## 'Though I'm an old man now'}

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:22.180
Katori-sen...

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:24.490
No, Mato-chan.

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:26.030
Peter.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:30.230
Why didn't you...

00:20:31.270 --> 00:20:33.020
tell me right away?!

00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:34.920
Ouch!

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:37.650
Hey, I thought it couldn't have been true either.

